1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,000
= kissasia.co =

2
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

3
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

4
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

5
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,902
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,071
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

7
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:53,950
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

8
00:01:13,053 --> 00:01:14,054
Thanks.

9
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,227
These photos...

10
00:01:20,310 --> 00:01:21,645
They're the victims.

11
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:24,189
Jo Nayeong.

12
00:01:25,857 --> 00:01:26,858
Choi Yeongmin.

13
00:01:30,862 --> 00:01:31,863
Kim Heejun.

14
00:01:34,866 --> 00:01:37,536
Jo Nayeong and Choi Yeongmin
were amateur models,

15
00:01:37,619 --> 00:01:40,288
and they went missing the day
after they met Yu Seongwon.

16
00:01:42,207 --> 00:01:44,167
So I was watching Yu Seongwon.

17
00:01:44,251 --> 00:01:45,961
SEPTEMBER 14, 2021

18
00:01:51,258 --> 00:01:52,342
[knock on car window]

19
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:55,345
You're a detective, right?

20
00:01:56,888 --> 00:01:58,265
Can I get in?

21
00:02:06,356 --> 00:02:08,108
What did Seongwon do?

22
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,318
Why do you ask?

23
00:02:10,402 --> 00:02:11,945
Because I'm curious.

24
00:02:12,028 --> 00:02:14,448
I'm really close with him.
[inhales sharply]

25
00:02:14,531 --> 00:02:15,824
But how should I put this?

26
00:02:15,907 --> 00:02:18,201
Sometimes he seems a little crazy.

27
00:02:18,285 --> 00:02:21,288
The other day, while having a drink,
he said something strange.

28
00:02:22,581 --> 00:02:23,582
What did he say?

29
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:28,044
That he wanted to use
a corpse as his model.

30
00:02:28,670 --> 00:02:31,673
He said if the model moves
while he's feeling inspired,

31
00:02:31,757 --> 00:02:32,841
he wants to kill them.

32
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,845
I heard his models disappeared.

33
00:02:37,554 --> 00:02:38,555
Is it true?

34
00:02:42,058 --> 00:02:43,185
Can I have your number?

35
00:02:51,109 --> 00:02:52,861
GANGHA POLICE
DETECTIVE JOO HYERA

36
00:02:52,944 --> 00:02:55,197
I'll let you know
if he does anything suspicious.

37
00:02:55,864 --> 00:02:56,865
Wait.

38
00:02:57,908 --> 00:03:00,327
It's too dangerous. Stay away from him.

39
00:03:01,203 --> 00:03:03,371
I've got good instincts.

40
00:03:03,455 --> 00:03:04,581
I'll keep you updated.

41
00:03:10,212 --> 00:03:11,963
[Hyera] Kim Heejun
went missing after that.

42
00:03:13,507 --> 00:03:15,091
And Yu Seongwon moved to the UK.

43
00:03:19,054 --> 00:03:23,058
I believe Yu Seongwon made that piece
after killing Kim Heejun,

44
00:03:26,853 --> 00:03:29,523
to put his murder on display.

45
00:03:32,275 --> 00:03:34,027
He wants to show off

46
00:03:35,153 --> 00:03:36,613
that he's the killer.

47
00:03:40,116 --> 00:03:41,243
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

48
00:03:51,503 --> 00:03:53,421
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

49
00:03:53,505 --> 00:03:56,883
I couldn't pinpoint
where the other victims had been murdered,

50
00:03:59,219 --> 00:04:01,346
but Kim Heejun likely died
in a field of reeds.

51
00:04:01,429 --> 00:04:03,348
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

52
00:04:03,431 --> 00:04:05,058
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

53
00:04:05,141 --> 00:04:07,352
He left a clue in his artwork on purpose.

54
00:04:08,103 --> 00:04:10,689
Because he's become certain
he'd never get caught.

55
00:04:10,772 --> 00:04:12,023
[Isoo sighs softly]

56
00:04:13,233 --> 00:04:14,693
DALSEONG WETLAND

57
00:04:14,776 --> 00:04:17,279
YEONGSAN RIVER GARDEN

58
00:04:18,613 --> 00:04:20,198
Is that why you collected these?

59
00:04:20,282 --> 00:04:21,283
[Hyera] Yes.

60
00:04:21,366 --> 00:04:22,367
GAPCHEON WETLAND

61
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:24,786
I need to find out
where the murder happened

62
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:28,123
to at least recover the body.

63
00:04:31,209 --> 00:04:32,711
Will you help me?

64
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,722
[♪ tense, suspenseful music continues]

65
00:04:51,313 --> 00:04:52,898
EPISODE 9

66
00:05:00,155 --> 00:05:01,239
[Isoo sighs softly]

67
00:05:06,411 --> 00:05:08,204
[chuckles] Young Master.

68
00:05:08,288 --> 00:05:11,166
Gosh, you're still calling me
"Young Master."

69
00:05:11,249 --> 00:05:13,293
Have you been well? It's been a while.

70
00:05:13,376 --> 00:05:15,003
It's good to see you again.

71
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:17,005
Seongwon is inside, isn't he?

72
00:05:17,088 --> 00:05:19,049
Yes. Please go ahead.

73
00:05:19,132 --> 00:05:21,092
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

74
00:05:47,702 --> 00:05:48,703
[Seongwon] Oh!

75
00:05:49,496 --> 00:05:50,497
Isoo!

76
00:05:51,581 --> 00:05:54,501
Hey, what are you doing here?
You didn't even call.

77
00:05:54,584 --> 00:05:55,794
I was just passing by.

78
00:05:56,962 --> 00:05:58,797
You missed me, didn't you? [chuckles]

79
00:06:00,006 --> 00:06:01,841
What's that? A gift?

80
00:06:01,925 --> 00:06:03,093
Yeah.

81
00:06:03,176 --> 00:06:05,595
It's the whiskey I made.

82
00:06:07,764 --> 00:06:08,807
Wait here a second.

83
00:06:09,474 --> 00:06:11,101
Mr. Hwang!

84
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:12,978
Do we have any fruit?

85
00:06:13,061 --> 00:06:15,313
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

86
00:06:45,301 --> 00:06:46,302
[♪ music fades]

87
00:06:46,386 --> 00:06:47,429
[exhales contentedly]

88
00:06:48,304 --> 00:06:50,890
Wow. Did you really make this?

89
00:06:50,974 --> 00:06:52,642
Of course I did.

90
00:06:52,726 --> 00:06:54,352
This is a work of art.

91
00:06:54,436 --> 00:06:55,437
-Cheers.
-[chuckles]

92
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,855
[clink]

93
00:07:01,025 --> 00:07:02,360
By the way, that piece there.

94
00:07:02,986 --> 00:07:04,237
What does it mean?

95
00:07:05,405 --> 00:07:06,489
[Seongwon] Mmm?

96
00:07:06,573 --> 00:07:09,117
[Isoo] What's with the pebbles
and why stick the reed in?

97
00:07:10,493 --> 00:07:12,203
I just don't get it.

98
00:07:14,998 --> 00:07:15,999
Why do you ask?

99
00:07:16,082 --> 00:07:17,959
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

100
00:07:18,042 --> 00:07:19,377
It's a secret.

101
00:07:24,591 --> 00:07:25,592
You...

102
00:07:25,675 --> 00:07:28,511
[exclaims incredulously] You're acting
like I know nothing about art again.

103
00:07:28,595 --> 00:07:30,722
Forget it. Don't tell me
if you don't want to.

104
00:07:30,805 --> 00:07:32,307
[chuckles] No, it's fine.

105
00:07:32,390 --> 00:07:33,808
I'll make an exception for you.

106
00:07:35,143 --> 00:07:36,519
[Seongwon] Mmm...

107
00:07:40,607 --> 00:07:42,066
For me,

108
00:07:43,443 --> 00:07:45,612
there are moments I could never forget.

109
00:07:47,572 --> 00:07:50,575
Moments I can recall
down to every last detail.

110
00:07:52,744 --> 00:07:53,912
The sunlight that day,

111
00:07:55,038 --> 00:07:56,581
the smell of the air,

112
00:07:57,791 --> 00:07:59,542
it's all in my head.

113
00:08:04,964 --> 00:08:07,050
The moment I first met you is one of them.

114
00:08:07,133 --> 00:08:08,218
[♪ music fades]

115
00:08:08,843 --> 00:08:09,844
Me?

116
00:08:11,596 --> 00:08:12,680
At the gathering?

117
00:08:14,933 --> 00:08:17,852
You don't remember, do you?

118
00:08:19,771 --> 00:08:21,105
We met way before that.

119
00:08:21,815 --> 00:08:23,441
When I was just a kid.

120
00:08:23,525 --> 00:08:25,318
I've liked you ever since then.

121
00:08:28,863 --> 00:08:29,989
That piece

122
00:08:30,865 --> 00:08:32,951
is a memory of one of those moments.

123
00:08:33,034 --> 00:08:35,036
[♪ ominous music playing]

124
00:08:35,119 --> 00:08:37,080
In a field of reeds in early winter,

125
00:08:38,498 --> 00:08:41,501
I'm walking forward,
stepping over the gravel.

126
00:08:49,425 --> 00:08:51,010
It was drizzling that day.

127
00:08:59,811 --> 00:09:01,020
[Heejun] Seongwon.

128
00:09:28,965 --> 00:09:31,301
I made that piece to remember that moment.

129
00:09:42,478 --> 00:09:43,646
[♪ music fades]

130
00:09:47,984 --> 00:09:49,777
I met Seongwon yesterday.

131
00:09:50,862 --> 00:09:51,863
What do you think?

132
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,908
I don't know if he's the real killer,

133
00:09:54,991 --> 00:09:55,992
but here.

134
00:09:58,203 --> 00:09:59,746
I took it from that sculpture.

135
00:09:59,829 --> 00:10:00,955
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

136
00:10:04,584 --> 00:10:05,752
By the way,

137
00:10:07,212 --> 00:10:09,088
there was a kiln in his studio.

138
00:10:11,549 --> 00:10:12,842
A kiln?

139
00:10:14,219 --> 00:10:16,638
If he burned the bodies there...

140
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:18,348
We won't find any DNA.

141
00:10:20,391 --> 00:10:21,559
[sighs]

142
00:10:21,643 --> 00:10:23,144
I'll look into this first.

143
00:10:23,853 --> 00:10:24,854
Also,

144
00:10:26,648 --> 00:10:28,233
he said it was raining that day.

145
00:10:30,568 --> 00:10:32,528
The day he found inspiration
for that piece.

146
00:10:32,612 --> 00:10:33,947
[♪ music swells]

147
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:38,576
[♪ music fades]

148
00:10:39,744 --> 00:10:41,663
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

149
00:10:54,342 --> 00:10:56,719
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

150
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:07,689
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
MOON SEYEON

151
00:11:13,444 --> 00:11:14,570
[♪ music fades]

152
00:11:14,654 --> 00:11:16,406
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

153
00:11:21,494 --> 00:11:23,204
[blade swooshing]

154
00:11:47,937 --> 00:11:49,147
[♪ music stops]

155
00:11:49,605 --> 00:11:51,357
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

156
00:11:58,614 --> 00:12:00,241
[♪ music turns ominous]

157
00:12:05,621 --> 00:12:07,457
[♪ music swells, fades]

158
00:12:08,041 --> 00:12:09,125
[exhales softly]

159
00:12:11,252 --> 00:12:12,295
[sniffles]

160
00:12:17,133 --> 00:12:18,718
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

161
00:12:18,801 --> 00:12:20,303
[blade swooshing]

162
00:12:42,867 --> 00:12:44,577
[♪ music turns suspenseful]

163
00:12:47,538 --> 00:12:49,082
[panting]

164
00:12:50,249 --> 00:12:53,127
[girl, weakly] Please... help me.

165
00:12:54,337 --> 00:12:56,089
[♪ ominous music playing]

166
00:13:03,763 --> 00:13:05,139
[sword clatters]

167
00:13:08,476 --> 00:13:09,769
[Seyeon] Don't come any closer.

168
00:13:09,852 --> 00:13:11,729
Stay away from me!

169
00:13:11,813 --> 00:13:13,731
[screaming]

170
00:13:13,815 --> 00:13:15,274
Go away!

171
00:13:15,358 --> 00:13:16,567
[♪ music swells, fades]

172
00:13:16,651 --> 00:13:17,819
[scream echoes, fades]

173
00:13:23,533 --> 00:13:25,284
[students chattering]

174
00:13:36,671 --> 00:13:37,672
DANCE STUDIO 1

175
00:13:40,091 --> 00:13:41,175
[all scream]

176
00:13:41,259 --> 00:13:42,760
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

177
00:13:42,844 --> 00:13:43,845
Oh, my God.

178
00:13:44,470 --> 00:13:46,347
[students whispering anxiously]

179
00:13:46,430 --> 00:13:47,807
Why aren't you girls going in?

180
00:13:47,890 --> 00:13:48,933
[student] Ms. Jeong.

181
00:13:50,268 --> 00:13:51,269
What?

182
00:13:55,398 --> 00:13:57,150
[♪ music increases in tempo]

183
00:13:59,944 --> 00:14:01,028
[Juhee gasps]

184
00:14:01,112 --> 00:14:02,321
[♪ music swells]

185
00:14:03,781 --> 00:14:04,782
[♪ music fades]

186
00:14:04,866 --> 00:14:06,742
[siren blaring]

187
00:14:11,747 --> 00:14:12,915
[brakes squeal]

188
00:14:13,833 --> 00:14:14,917
[siren stops blaring]

189
00:14:30,766 --> 00:14:32,727
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

190
00:14:41,986 --> 00:14:43,738
-[Isoo] How did this happen?
-[♪ music fades]

191
00:14:43,821 --> 00:14:45,823
Let's check if anyone's been in or out.

192
00:14:45,907 --> 00:14:46,908
Got it.

193
00:14:55,208 --> 00:14:56,209
[sighs softly]

194
00:14:58,461 --> 00:15:00,004
[♪ soft melancholy music playing]

195
00:15:02,715 --> 00:15:05,301
-[audio distorts]
-[slow, muffled thuds]

196
00:15:05,384 --> 00:15:07,511
[high-pitched tone droning, intensifies]

197
00:15:09,138 --> 00:15:11,057
-[high-pitched tone fades]
-[audio normalizes]

198
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:12,683
[♪ soft melancholy music continues]

199
00:15:20,816 --> 00:15:21,901
Please have a look.

200
00:15:25,696 --> 00:15:26,697
[dispenser clicks]

201
00:15:27,198 --> 00:15:28,241
[exhales heavily]

202
00:15:33,496 --> 00:15:35,873
[Isoo breathing heavily]

203
00:15:40,419 --> 00:15:41,420
[Hyera] What's wrong?

204
00:15:44,257 --> 00:15:45,258
[panting] Uh...

205
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,510
I was just thirsty.

206
00:15:49,178 --> 00:15:50,179
[exhales heavily]

207
00:15:51,639 --> 00:15:53,140
-[continues panting]
-[♪ music fades]

208
00:15:54,141 --> 00:15:55,142
[knock at door]

209
00:15:57,561 --> 00:15:59,230
We're from Gangha Police Station.

210
00:15:59,313 --> 00:16:00,898
Who is the deceased student?

211
00:16:02,233 --> 00:16:03,818
Her name is Moon Seyeon.

212
00:16:03,901 --> 00:16:05,069
I'm her homeroom teacher.

213
00:16:05,945 --> 00:16:08,447
When did you last see her?

214
00:16:08,531 --> 00:16:09,573
Uh...

215
00:16:09,657 --> 00:16:10,950
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

216
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:12,576
When school let out at 5:00 p.m.

217
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,161
But

218
00:16:14,245 --> 00:16:17,123
she said she was going to rehearse
in the practice room from 9:00.

219
00:16:17,665 --> 00:16:19,125
Nine o'clock at night?

220
00:16:19,625 --> 00:16:20,626
Yes.

221
00:16:20,710 --> 00:16:23,129
Is the practice room
used at night as well?

222
00:16:24,005 --> 00:16:25,047
Uh...

223
00:16:25,131 --> 00:16:27,508
Seyeon is the lead dancer
in the arts festival,

224
00:16:27,591 --> 00:16:29,844
so she was allowed to use it anytime.

225
00:16:29,927 --> 00:16:31,095
Allowed by whom?

226
00:16:32,388 --> 00:16:33,723
The principal.

227
00:16:34,724 --> 00:16:38,227
Seyeon was personally instructed
by the principal.

228
00:16:40,021 --> 00:16:42,523
Do the teachers stay late
at school with her?

229
00:16:42,606 --> 00:16:44,650
No, we go home for the day.

230
00:16:45,401 --> 00:16:48,946
The principal sometimes stays behind
to help Seyeon with practice,

231
00:16:50,072 --> 00:16:51,490
but she left early yesterday.

232
00:16:51,574 --> 00:16:54,535
Then who is at school late at night?

233
00:16:54,618 --> 00:16:56,954
The security guard on night duty.

234
00:16:58,414 --> 00:17:00,166
-Check with the security office.
-[both] Okay.

235
00:17:00,249 --> 00:17:02,126
[♪ music swells, fades]

236
00:17:05,963 --> 00:17:08,299
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

237
00:17:08,382 --> 00:17:10,092
GRAND PRIZE

238
00:17:10,176 --> 00:17:12,219
AWARD CERTIFICATE

239
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:16,599
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

240
00:17:19,643 --> 00:17:20,686
[♪ music fades]

241
00:17:20,770 --> 00:17:21,771
[knock at door]

242
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:24,398
2025 JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL

243
00:17:25,274 --> 00:17:27,068
[Isoo] We're from Gangha Police Station.

244
00:17:28,069 --> 00:17:29,195
[gasps]

245
00:17:29,695 --> 00:17:32,114
PRINCIPAL OF JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
JEONG JOOHEE

246
00:17:32,198 --> 00:17:34,033
Aren't you the dancer Jeong Joohee?

247
00:17:36,077 --> 00:17:37,078
You know me?

248
00:17:37,161 --> 00:17:39,622
Of course. I even went
to your performance in New York.

249
00:17:39,705 --> 00:17:41,123
It's an honor.

250
00:17:42,625 --> 00:17:43,626
[chuckles softly]

251
00:17:44,126 --> 00:17:45,127
She's famous.

252
00:17:45,795 --> 00:17:48,255
A living legend of Korean dance.

253
00:17:48,339 --> 00:17:51,050
[chuckles softly] You're too kind.
It's all in the past.

254
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:54,595
This is my team leader.
She doesn't get out much.

255
00:17:54,679 --> 00:17:58,432
-She knows nothing about the arts.
-I'm Joo Hyera with Gangha Police.

256
00:17:58,891 --> 00:18:00,476
Uh, I'm Jin Isoo.

257
00:18:00,559 --> 00:18:01,852
Right, yes.

258
00:18:02,436 --> 00:18:03,646
Please have a seat.

259
00:18:04,230 --> 00:18:05,523
[Isoo exhales in awe]

260
00:18:06,649 --> 00:18:08,067
CERTIFICATE OF APPOINTMENT

261
00:18:08,150 --> 00:18:10,903
Oh, so you became a principal.

262
00:18:11,487 --> 00:18:13,739
I had some health issues.

263
00:18:13,823 --> 00:18:16,534
Now I devote my time to teaching students.

264
00:18:16,617 --> 00:18:19,286
Oh. They're lucky
to be learning from a legend.

265
00:18:19,370 --> 00:18:20,955
[chuckles softly] Not at all.

266
00:18:21,038 --> 00:18:22,665
I appreciate your kind words.

267
00:18:23,290 --> 00:18:27,211
We're here because of Moon Seyeon.
You know what happened, right?

268
00:18:27,294 --> 00:18:28,921
[breath trembles] Yes.

269
00:18:29,004 --> 00:18:30,172
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

270
00:18:30,256 --> 00:18:31,257
[exhales heavily]

271
00:18:31,716 --> 00:18:33,801
I was so shocked
at the studio this morning.

272
00:18:34,552 --> 00:18:37,346
We heard you personally instructed Seyeon.

273
00:18:38,431 --> 00:18:40,933
She was a very talented student.

274
00:18:42,184 --> 00:18:45,062
She had the potential
to become a great dancer.

275
00:18:45,855 --> 00:18:48,107
Was Seyeon at school
by herself last night?

276
00:18:48,190 --> 00:18:49,191
[Juhee] Yes.

277
00:18:49,275 --> 00:18:52,069
She was scheduled
to practice on her own yesterday.

278
00:18:52,570 --> 00:18:54,530
The arts festival is
just around the corner,

279
00:18:54,613 --> 00:18:57,533
so she worked very hard,
practicing every day without fail.

280
00:18:58,784 --> 00:19:00,703
[Hyera breathes deeply]

281
00:19:00,786 --> 00:19:04,540
Was there anyone
who didn't get along with Seyeon?

282
00:19:04,623 --> 00:19:06,333
Teacher or student, anyone at all.

283
00:19:06,959 --> 00:19:07,960
I'm not sure.

284
00:19:08,794 --> 00:19:10,838
She wasn't a difficult person,

285
00:19:10,921 --> 00:19:12,673
and she was an outgoing, sweet girl.

286
00:19:13,507 --> 00:19:15,384
She was the lead dancer of the festival,

287
00:19:15,468 --> 00:19:18,262
and she was personally taught by you.

288
00:19:18,345 --> 00:19:21,265
Someone might have been jealous of her.

289
00:19:21,348 --> 00:19:23,184
That happens all the time.

290
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:26,353
All my students
are ambitious and passionate.

291
00:19:26,979 --> 00:19:30,357
Being jealous and competitive
is part of how you grow, isn't it?

292
00:19:30,441 --> 00:19:31,692
That's true.

293
00:19:31,776 --> 00:19:34,195
But killing someone for that reason?

294
00:19:34,862 --> 00:19:36,864
There's no one like that at our school.

295
00:19:40,159 --> 00:19:41,160
[♪ music fades]

296
00:19:41,243 --> 00:19:43,120
I was on duty yesterday.

297
00:19:43,204 --> 00:19:45,790
I went home this morning,
but came back after I got the call.

298
00:19:45,873 --> 00:19:48,667
Did you see
the deceased student last night?

299
00:19:48,751 --> 00:19:52,296
Yes, she came in around 9:00 p.m.

300
00:19:52,379 --> 00:19:54,340
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

301
00:19:58,844 --> 00:20:00,471
She's been coming every night.

302
00:20:01,138 --> 00:20:03,265
Did you notice anything unusual?

303
00:20:03,349 --> 00:20:04,600
Like anyone following her?

304
00:20:04,683 --> 00:20:08,103
No, she went inside
and I locked the gate right away.

305
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:12,399
Was that the last time you saw her?

306
00:20:12,483 --> 00:20:15,194
I last saw her
when I was making my round at 10:00 p.m.

307
00:20:15,277 --> 00:20:16,987
She was practicing alone.

308
00:20:17,071 --> 00:20:19,156
[♪ muffled percussive folk music plays]

309
00:20:24,662 --> 00:20:26,747
Did you notice anything unusual then?

310
00:20:27,665 --> 00:20:28,666
Like I said, no.

311
00:20:28,749 --> 00:20:31,293
Did you check inside all the classrooms?

312
00:20:31,377 --> 00:20:34,380
Well, not really,
but all the classrooms were locked.

313
00:20:34,463 --> 00:20:37,675
There really was no one there.
I have no idea how this happened.

314
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:40,302
[♪ music fades]

315
00:20:40,886 --> 00:20:42,972
Could you copy
all the security footage onto this?

316
00:20:43,055 --> 00:20:44,056
[softly] Sure.

317
00:20:46,559 --> 00:20:48,394
What's going to happen to me?

318
00:20:48,477 --> 00:20:49,937
Will I get in trouble for this?

319
00:20:50,521 --> 00:20:52,147
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

320
00:20:53,566 --> 00:20:55,401
Why would you worry about that?

321
00:20:55,484 --> 00:20:59,446
I'm just worried
I might get blamed for this.

322
00:21:00,447 --> 00:21:02,616
You'll be fine
if you've done nothing wrong.

323
00:21:03,576 --> 00:21:04,660
[sighs wearily]

324
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:14,211
CHANGING ROOM

325
00:21:14,295 --> 00:21:15,588
[♪ music swells]

326
00:21:20,759 --> 00:21:21,844
[♪ music fades]

327
00:21:22,469 --> 00:21:24,680
-Let's visit the victim's home first.
-Okay.

328
00:21:25,973 --> 00:21:26,974
Oh.

329
00:21:27,057 --> 00:21:28,601
-Mmm. Delicious.
-[Isoo] It's bungeoppang.

330
00:21:29,226 --> 00:21:30,352
I've wanted to try that.

331
00:21:31,228 --> 00:21:32,688
Have you never had bungeoppang?

332
00:21:32,771 --> 00:21:34,356
They don't sell it near my place.

333
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:37,026
-[chuckles softly] Go get some.
-Really?

334
00:21:37,651 --> 00:21:38,819
Nice!

335
00:21:39,486 --> 00:21:41,530
-Be quick.
-Okay, got it.

336
00:21:41,614 --> 00:21:42,698
Where do you buy those?

337
00:21:44,033 --> 00:21:45,034
Where's Isoo going?

338
00:21:45,618 --> 00:21:46,744
To get bungeoppang.

339
00:21:46,827 --> 00:21:48,454
-He's never had it before.
-What?

340
00:21:48,954 --> 00:21:51,707
[scoffs] He surprisingly hasn't tried
a lot of things.

341
00:21:51,790 --> 00:21:53,667
What did the security guard say?

342
00:21:53,751 --> 00:21:56,253
He last saw her
while making his rounds at 10:00 p.m.

343
00:21:56,337 --> 00:21:58,172
He didn't see anyone suspicious.

344
00:21:59,965 --> 00:22:01,800
[breathes deeply]

345
00:22:03,093 --> 00:22:04,762
-There you go.
-[students] Thank you.

346
00:22:04,845 --> 00:22:05,930
-[vendor] Bye.
-Hello.

347
00:22:06,013 --> 00:22:07,014
[♪ jaunty music playing]

348
00:22:07,097 --> 00:22:08,140
[softly] Oh...

349
00:22:08,223 --> 00:22:09,642
PIZZA, SPICY

350
00:22:09,725 --> 00:22:11,018
LOW SUGAR CUSTARD, RED BEAN

351
00:22:11,769 --> 00:22:13,979
Excuse me, what's the "custard" flavor?

352
00:22:14,772 --> 00:22:16,440
It's filled with custard cream.

353
00:22:16,523 --> 00:22:17,733
Oh!

354
00:22:17,816 --> 00:22:20,319
Then I'll take four of each flavor.

355
00:22:20,402 --> 00:22:22,237
Coming right up.

356
00:22:24,448 --> 00:22:26,283
NO CARD, CASH ONLY
BANK TRANSFER DETAILS

357
00:22:26,367 --> 00:22:28,202
Don't you take card?

358
00:22:28,285 --> 00:22:29,662
You can pay by bank transfer.

359
00:22:29,745 --> 00:22:31,830
-Bank transfer?
-[vendor] Yes.

360
00:22:31,914 --> 00:22:32,957
Bank transfer.

361
00:22:33,958 --> 00:22:34,959
[♪ music fades]

362
00:22:35,042 --> 00:22:37,378
I'm sure Moon Seyeon died
because of the curse.

363
00:22:37,461 --> 00:22:39,922
[student] That curse was real.

364
00:22:40,005 --> 00:22:41,757
You think that girl really killed her?

365
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,759
Why else did she die in the practice room?

366
00:22:43,842 --> 00:22:44,843
What do you mean?

367
00:22:45,886 --> 00:22:46,887
A curse?

368
00:22:47,805 --> 00:22:49,515
-Girls.
-Here, all packed up for you.

369
00:22:49,598 --> 00:22:52,017
-Please transfer the money.
-Right, bank transfer.

370
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:54,144
Girls!

371
00:22:54,228 --> 00:22:56,355
Don't go.
I'll buy you custard bungeoppang!

372
00:22:56,689 --> 00:22:57,690
[sighs]

373
00:23:01,151 --> 00:23:02,236
By the way,

374
00:23:03,278 --> 00:23:04,863
the students said something weird.

375
00:23:04,947 --> 00:23:06,281
Like what?

376
00:23:06,865 --> 00:23:08,701
That Seyeon died from a curse.

377
00:23:08,784 --> 00:23:10,744
-A curse?
-[Isoo] Yeah.

378
00:23:10,828 --> 00:23:13,247
They said she was cursed
and died in the practice room.

379
00:23:13,330 --> 00:23:15,249
-Really?
-Yeah.

380
00:23:20,129 --> 00:23:21,130
Mmm.

381
00:23:21,630 --> 00:23:22,631
Personally,

382
00:23:25,175 --> 00:23:26,593
I prefer red bean.

383
00:23:26,677 --> 00:23:28,387
[♪ jaunty music playing]

384
00:23:28,470 --> 00:23:30,097
I'm trying to be serious here.

385
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:32,266
-I prefer custard.
-[Kyungjin, muffled] I prefer red bean.

386
00:23:34,184 --> 00:23:35,185
Really?

387
00:23:37,062 --> 00:23:38,105
[♪ music fades]

388
00:23:38,188 --> 00:23:40,190
SEWON HOSPITAL

389
00:23:43,861 --> 00:23:45,446
[footsteps approaching]

390
00:23:45,529 --> 00:23:46,655
[Dr. Jinkyung] Hello.

391
00:23:46,739 --> 00:23:47,865
[chuckles]

392
00:23:47,948 --> 00:23:49,408
It's been a while.

393
00:23:49,491 --> 00:23:50,492
Hello.

394
00:23:50,993 --> 00:23:52,661
Did you have chemotherapy?

395
00:23:52,745 --> 00:23:53,996
-Yes.
-[chuckles softly]

396
00:23:54,997 --> 00:23:56,707
How are you feeling?

397
00:23:56,790 --> 00:23:59,001
Much better, thanks to you.

398
00:23:59,084 --> 00:24:00,335
I'm glad to hear that.

399
00:24:00,419 --> 00:24:03,380
I thought you were sitting here
because you weren't feeling well.

400
00:24:03,464 --> 00:24:04,923
I was just

401
00:24:05,507 --> 00:24:09,344
thinking I might live
a little differently from now on.

402
00:24:09,428 --> 00:24:11,138
Differently? In what way?

403
00:24:12,389 --> 00:24:16,185
I originally planned to retire
last year and travel the world.

404
00:24:16,268 --> 00:24:17,603
Travel the world?

405
00:24:18,187 --> 00:24:20,439
It's nothing grand,

406
00:24:20,522 --> 00:24:23,233
but I've only ever
traveled abroad for work.

407
00:24:23,317 --> 00:24:24,318
[♪ melancholy music playing]

408
00:24:24,401 --> 00:24:26,320
Ah, you must've led quite a busy life.
[chuckles]

409
00:24:26,403 --> 00:24:27,404
[chuckles]

410
00:24:28,030 --> 00:24:29,448
Traveling the world.

411
00:24:30,532 --> 00:24:31,784
That sounds nice.

412
00:24:32,242 --> 00:24:35,329
I'm actually starting
my sabbatical next month.

413
00:24:36,163 --> 00:24:39,249
I was thinking of taking a trip, too.

414
00:24:39,333 --> 00:24:40,834
Sabbatical?

415
00:24:41,543 --> 00:24:42,753
That's nice.

416
00:24:43,879 --> 00:24:47,382
I can't even remember the last time
I did nothing and just relaxed.

417
00:24:48,175 --> 00:24:51,428
[sighs deeply] Time really flies,
doesn't it? [chuckles]

418
00:24:52,554 --> 00:24:54,473
-It does.
-[chuckles]

419
00:24:59,812 --> 00:25:01,355
[♪ melancholy music continues]

420
00:25:08,695 --> 00:25:11,073
[breath trembles] My daughter

421
00:25:12,324 --> 00:25:14,868
got divorced when Seyeon was little,

422
00:25:16,662 --> 00:25:18,413
then passed away young.

423
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:23,544
So I raised Seyeon on my own.

424
00:25:26,130 --> 00:25:28,382
[sniffles, breathes deeply]

425
00:25:28,465 --> 00:25:31,969
She was such a sweet and lovely girl.

426
00:25:32,052 --> 00:25:35,097
Ever since she was little,
whenever she heard any music,

427
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:38,934
she would dance beautifully
like a fairy, like an angel.

428
00:25:41,395 --> 00:25:43,689
She said she'd become a famous dancer...

429
00:25:44,731 --> 00:25:48,777
[voice shaking] ...and take good care
of her grandma. [sobbing]

430
00:25:53,073 --> 00:25:56,160
As her grandmother, I had no money,

431
00:25:56,952 --> 00:25:58,370
no power.

432
00:25:58,912 --> 00:26:02,124
[sniffles]
Even though that poor child was sick,

433
00:26:02,916 --> 00:26:05,544
she worked part-time
while going to school.

434
00:26:08,213 --> 00:26:10,883
Was she unwell?

435
00:26:11,842 --> 00:26:13,719
She had asthma.

436
00:26:13,802 --> 00:26:15,679
[breath trembling]

437
00:26:16,471 --> 00:26:19,349
But she still went to practice every day

438
00:26:19,433 --> 00:26:22,144
and even got the lead role
in the arts festival.

439
00:26:22,227 --> 00:26:24,062
How could this happen? [sobbing]

440
00:26:30,944 --> 00:26:33,155
Could we look around Seyeon's room?

441
00:26:34,323 --> 00:26:35,324
Yes.

442
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:47,586
-[continues sobbing]
-[door opens]

443
00:26:50,714 --> 00:26:52,257
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

444
00:27:00,724 --> 00:27:02,893
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

445
00:27:05,646 --> 00:27:07,314
AWARD CERTIFICATE

446
00:27:26,208 --> 00:27:27,709
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

447
00:27:28,210 --> 00:27:29,211
Look at this.

448
00:27:29,294 --> 00:27:30,796
[♪ music increases in tempo]

449
00:27:34,257 --> 00:27:35,801
Is this the curse?

450
00:27:41,765 --> 00:27:44,476
[Hyera] Do you know what this is?

451
00:27:44,559 --> 00:27:45,602
What's this?

452
00:27:47,145 --> 00:27:49,147
It was in her desk drawer.

453
00:27:49,815 --> 00:27:51,483
[Grandma, gasps shakily] Did someone

454
00:27:51,566 --> 00:27:55,404
hate my granddaughter this much?

455
00:27:55,904 --> 00:27:57,781
[sobbing] Why?

456
00:27:59,449 --> 00:28:00,993
[♪ music swells]

457
00:28:07,457 --> 00:28:10,002
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

458
00:28:10,085 --> 00:28:11,169
[♪ music fades]

459
00:28:14,047 --> 00:28:16,258
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

460
00:28:16,883 --> 00:28:17,884
[Kyungjin] Hey!

461
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:20,470
[laughing maniacally]

462
00:28:26,143 --> 00:28:27,144
What's with him?

463
00:28:27,227 --> 00:28:29,604
[Kyungjin continues laughing maniacally]

464
00:28:29,688 --> 00:28:31,106
His girlfriend dumped him.

465
00:28:31,189 --> 00:28:32,482
[in English] What?

466
00:28:32,566 --> 00:28:34,234
Apparently,
it's a first for him.

467
00:28:35,444 --> 00:28:37,070
[in Korean] How did a dating expert
get dumped?

468
00:28:37,904 --> 00:28:38,989
Nobody

469
00:28:39,740 --> 00:28:41,575
-can bat a thousand.
-[cell phone vibrating]

470
00:28:43,410 --> 00:28:44,619
[Isoo exhales deeply]

471
00:28:46,872 --> 00:28:48,040
Hello, Jiwon?

472
00:28:49,750 --> 00:28:50,959
[♪ music fades]

473
00:28:51,043 --> 00:28:53,170
-Did something happen?
-No, it's nothing.

474
00:28:53,795 --> 00:28:55,756
-Did you find anything?
-Not yet.

475
00:28:56,381 --> 00:28:59,259
I played it back from 9:00 p.m.,
but no one went into the building.

476
00:29:00,177 --> 00:29:02,179
[Isoo] You need to look carefully,
Kyungjin.

477
00:29:02,971 --> 00:29:06,016
Our suspect is hiding deep in the shadows.

478
00:29:06,516 --> 00:29:07,517
What?

479
00:29:08,602 --> 00:29:10,562
Remember the Han Yura case? The candles.

480
00:29:10,645 --> 00:29:11,646
The candles.

481
00:29:12,230 --> 00:29:13,940
The key to this case is the curse.

482
00:29:14,733 --> 00:29:17,486
A vengeful presence might've been
caught on camera. Play it.

483
00:29:17,569 --> 00:29:18,779
[scoffs softly]

484
00:29:22,616 --> 00:29:23,658
[keyboard clacking]

485
00:29:23,742 --> 00:29:25,202
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

486
00:29:30,957 --> 00:29:32,959
Okay, I'll call you later.

487
00:29:33,043 --> 00:29:34,419
[♪ music fades]

488
00:29:35,087 --> 00:29:36,088
When's the autopsy?

489
00:29:36,171 --> 00:29:38,048
They're just starting now.

490
00:29:38,673 --> 00:29:40,759
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

491
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:50,519
[Dr. Yoon, sighs] One second.

492
00:29:51,561 --> 00:29:53,355
[camera shutter clicking]

493
00:29:55,816 --> 00:29:57,609
[♪ music increases in tempo]

494
00:30:10,539 --> 00:30:11,790
Do we have a time of death?

495
00:30:11,873 --> 00:30:14,126
Between 10:00 and 11:00 p.m.

496
00:30:15,627 --> 00:30:16,795
[sighs heavily]

497
00:30:17,546 --> 00:30:19,965
Then we can't rule out the security guard.

498
00:30:21,007 --> 00:30:22,259
[both gasp]

499
00:30:22,342 --> 00:30:23,552
[♪ music fades]

500
00:30:23,635 --> 00:30:24,678
[Isoo gasps softly]

501
00:30:24,761 --> 00:30:26,638
-Did you see that?
-Yes.

502
00:30:26,721 --> 00:30:28,306
What is it now?

503
00:30:29,850 --> 00:30:32,269
It's real.

504
00:30:32,811 --> 00:30:34,271
Here, look.

505
00:30:34,354 --> 00:30:36,148
[♪ ominous music playing]

506
00:30:36,606 --> 00:30:38,233
See? Right here.

507
00:30:38,942 --> 00:30:41,695
Three, two, one.

508
00:30:41,778 --> 00:30:43,113
[♪ ominous sting]

509
00:30:43,196 --> 00:30:44,406
[♪ music fades]

510
00:30:44,990 --> 00:30:46,032
[Isoo exhales sharply]

511
00:30:47,242 --> 00:30:48,243
[sniffles]

512
00:30:48,326 --> 00:30:49,578
It's probably a reflection.

513
00:30:50,245 --> 00:30:52,497
Yeah, like the shadow of a tree.

514
00:30:52,581 --> 00:30:54,374
How is this the shadow of a tree?

515
00:30:54,457 --> 00:30:58,044
-It's dust. There's dust on the camera.
-Yeah, she's right.

516
00:30:58,128 --> 00:31:00,380
Hey, what kind of ghost
shows up on camera?

517
00:31:00,463 --> 00:31:03,633
Don't you know about spirit photography?
What kind of dust is that big?

518
00:31:03,717 --> 00:31:06,178
This looks way too much like a person.

519
00:31:06,261 --> 00:31:07,637
That's enough.

520
00:31:07,721 --> 00:31:09,639
I don't know
how that got caught on camera,

521
00:31:09,723 --> 00:31:12,809
but no ghost or curse can kill a person.

522
00:31:13,476 --> 00:31:14,853
How can you be so sure?

523
00:31:14,936 --> 00:31:17,147
The truth is out there.

524
00:31:17,230 --> 00:31:18,982
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

525
00:31:23,153 --> 00:31:24,905
Someone's vengeful spirit

526
00:31:25,739 --> 00:31:27,365
is haunting the school.

527
00:31:29,034 --> 00:31:30,035
A haunted arts school.

528
00:31:30,744 --> 00:31:32,579
[breath trembling, grunts]

529
00:31:34,039 --> 00:31:35,081
I'm scared.

530
00:31:35,165 --> 00:31:36,416
[♪ music fades]

531
00:31:36,499 --> 00:31:37,500
[gasps softly]

532
00:31:38,293 --> 00:31:39,628
Is it really dust?

533
00:31:42,714 --> 00:31:43,924
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

534
00:31:44,007 --> 00:31:47,052
You found this inside Seyeon's desk?

535
00:31:48,261 --> 00:31:49,512
[exhales in disbelief]

536
00:31:49,596 --> 00:31:51,014
Who would do such a thing?

537
00:31:51,097 --> 00:31:53,725
Someone despised Moon Seyeon.

538
00:31:54,935 --> 00:31:56,269
Does anyone come to mind?

539
00:31:57,062 --> 00:31:58,146
[exhales softly]

540
00:31:58,230 --> 00:32:00,607
[breathes deeply] I really don't know.

541
00:32:01,566 --> 00:32:06,196
Mmm, then do you know
who Seyeon's closest friend was?

542
00:32:09,699 --> 00:32:11,534
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

543
00:32:11,618 --> 00:32:13,662
[Hyera] We heard you were close to Seyeon.

544
00:32:13,745 --> 00:32:15,330
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
PARK DAHYE

545
00:32:15,413 --> 00:32:16,623
We had something to ask you.

546
00:32:17,749 --> 00:32:18,750
Okay.

547
00:32:22,545 --> 00:32:24,631
This was inside Seyeon's desk.

548
00:32:24,714 --> 00:32:26,383
[♪ music fades]

549
00:32:26,466 --> 00:32:27,926
Who do you think sent it?

550
00:32:28,885 --> 00:32:30,136
Anyone come to mind?

551
00:32:33,431 --> 00:32:35,892
You can be honest. It'll stay between us.

552
00:32:38,353 --> 00:32:41,147
There was an accident a week ago.

553
00:32:41,231 --> 00:32:42,524
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

554
00:32:42,607 --> 00:32:44,567
-An accident?
-[Dahye] Yes.

555
00:32:44,651 --> 00:32:47,529
Hayun fell and broke her arm.

556
00:32:49,114 --> 00:32:50,407
[grunts, groans]

557
00:32:50,490 --> 00:32:51,616
[whimpers]

558
00:32:55,287 --> 00:32:57,664
[groans, breathes heavily]

559
00:32:57,747 --> 00:32:59,874
[Dahye] I heard that Seyeon was behind it.

560
00:33:00,583 --> 00:33:02,544
Did Seyeon really push her?

561
00:33:02,627 --> 00:33:04,546
She said it wasn't her,

562
00:33:05,213 --> 00:33:06,673
but apparently, everyone saw it.

563
00:33:10,885 --> 00:33:12,595
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
KIM HAYUN

564
00:33:12,679 --> 00:33:15,473
Hayun, can you show us your arm?

565
00:33:19,728 --> 00:33:20,854
You're hurt.

566
00:33:22,105 --> 00:33:23,440
How did that happen?

567
00:33:24,065 --> 00:33:25,317
I just fell.

568
00:33:25,942 --> 00:33:27,360
We heard Seyeon pushed you.

569
00:33:27,444 --> 00:33:28,945
Is that why you sent this to her?

570
00:33:29,446 --> 00:33:30,947
What's this?

571
00:33:33,616 --> 00:33:34,868
I don't do stuff like this.

572
00:33:35,452 --> 00:33:37,078
Is it true that Seyeon pushed you?

573
00:33:37,162 --> 00:33:38,538
Yes.

574
00:33:38,621 --> 00:33:40,040
Why did she do it?

575
00:33:41,499 --> 00:33:43,960
She can't even dance,
but she got cocky about getting the lead,

576
00:33:44,044 --> 00:33:45,086
so I said something.

577
00:33:45,712 --> 00:33:46,713
What did you say?

578
00:33:46,796 --> 00:33:49,007
I asked if she'd bribed the principal.

579
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:50,216
What do you mean?

580
00:33:51,217 --> 00:33:53,303
There were always rumors about that.

581
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:56,306
About how the principal's
obsessed with money.

582
00:33:57,223 --> 00:33:58,308
If she wasn't paid off,

583
00:33:59,059 --> 00:34:00,977
why would she pick Seyeon to be the lead?

584
00:34:03,396 --> 00:34:04,898
This wasn't me.

585
00:34:06,816 --> 00:34:10,028
Song Gaeun's the one
who'd do something so immature.

586
00:34:10,737 --> 00:34:13,698
She's the one who really hated Seyeon.

587
00:34:16,534 --> 00:34:17,827
THIRD-YEAR DANCE STUDENT
SONG GAEUN

588
00:34:17,911 --> 00:34:18,953
[Isoo] Try opening it.

589
00:34:19,037 --> 00:34:20,538
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

590
00:34:23,750 --> 00:34:25,126
It was you.

591
00:34:27,087 --> 00:34:28,671
Why did you send this?

592
00:34:28,755 --> 00:34:30,131
Because I was pissed off.

593
00:34:31,299 --> 00:34:33,051
Based on talent, I should be the lead.

594
00:34:35,303 --> 00:34:37,639
But this is just something everyone does.

595
00:34:38,264 --> 00:34:41,101
Do you think the principal favored Seyeon?

596
00:34:41,726 --> 00:34:42,894
Isn't that obvious?

597
00:34:43,770 --> 00:34:45,230
She really wasn't talented.

598
00:34:45,313 --> 00:34:46,564
Why would she favor Seyeon?

599
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:49,109
How would I know?

600
00:34:49,192 --> 00:34:50,944
But Seyeon told me

601
00:34:51,736 --> 00:34:54,322
the principal has no choice
but to pick her for the lead.

602
00:34:54,406 --> 00:34:56,324
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

603
00:35:02,205 --> 00:35:05,208
In any case,
this case has nothing to do with me.

604
00:35:05,291 --> 00:35:07,460
She didn't die because of this note.

605
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:12,298
Why did you write that you curse her?
People don't usually say that.

606
00:35:12,966 --> 00:35:14,050
And what's this paper?

607
00:35:15,885 --> 00:35:17,554
I bought it at the Witch's Shop.

608
00:35:17,637 --> 00:35:19,347
It's a trend at school.

609
00:35:20,140 --> 00:35:21,141
Because of Baek Yuna.

610
00:35:21,891 --> 00:35:22,892
Baek Yuna?

611
00:35:22,976 --> 00:35:24,769
An upperclassman
who killed herself last year.

612
00:35:24,853 --> 00:35:26,896
Someone killed herself here?

613
00:35:26,980 --> 00:35:29,691
Yes, in the practice room.

614
00:35:29,774 --> 00:35:32,944
That's why all the girls are saying
that Baek Yuna killed Seyeon.

615
00:35:34,195 --> 00:35:35,822
Were they connected somehow?

616
00:35:36,448 --> 00:35:37,782
I wouldn't know.

617
00:35:39,325 --> 00:35:41,411
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

618
00:35:46,708 --> 00:35:49,461
[camera shutter clicking]

619
00:35:52,881 --> 00:35:54,507
[♪ music increases in tempo]

620
00:36:05,935 --> 00:36:07,812
[forensics officer] What is all this?

621
00:36:07,896 --> 00:36:09,647
[♪ music swells, fades]

622
00:36:09,731 --> 00:36:11,316
VICTIM, CRIME SCENE, PRACTICE ROOM

623
00:36:11,399 --> 00:36:14,027
We responded to the scene
in the Baek Yuna case.

624
00:36:15,612 --> 00:36:17,864
Was that the ghost of Baek Yuna?

625
00:36:19,157 --> 00:36:20,366
Ghost?

626
00:36:21,618 --> 00:36:22,619
At this school,

627
00:36:23,995 --> 00:36:26,206
Baek Yuna's ghost is
still wandering around.

628
00:36:26,790 --> 00:36:28,333
What's wrong with you?

629
00:36:28,416 --> 00:36:29,918
How did she die?

630
00:36:30,585 --> 00:36:31,753
It was a suicide.

631
00:36:31,836 --> 00:36:34,464
She cut an artery
in the practice room late at night.

632
00:36:34,547 --> 00:36:35,632
[♪ tense music playing]

633
00:36:35,715 --> 00:36:37,467
Any chance it was a murder?

634
00:36:37,550 --> 00:36:40,053
No one was on site
except the security guard.

635
00:36:40,428 --> 00:36:42,680
Ah, and the practice room was locked.

636
00:36:42,764 --> 00:36:44,057
What about security cameras?

637
00:36:44,140 --> 00:36:45,809
That's the problem.

638
00:36:45,892 --> 00:36:47,268
They were down.

639
00:36:47,352 --> 00:36:49,479
Why did she commit suicide?

640
00:36:49,562 --> 00:36:50,647
[inhales deeply]

641
00:36:50,730 --> 00:36:52,357
That's also a bit unclear,

642
00:36:53,066 --> 00:36:56,861
but she was on antidepressants
a month or two before the incident.

643
00:36:56,945 --> 00:36:58,071
Having said that,

644
00:36:59,072 --> 00:37:01,658
she did text her mother
before committing suicide.

645
00:37:02,242 --> 00:37:03,284
It said she was sorry.

646
00:37:03,368 --> 00:37:04,410
MOM, I'M SORRY

647
00:37:05,370 --> 00:37:08,039
Were there rumors
that the principal was taking bribes?

648
00:37:09,582 --> 00:37:11,292
Yes, there were.

649
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:14,212
The principal used to be a famous dancer,

650
00:37:14,295 --> 00:37:17,507
but she quit because of a slipped disc
and returned to her old school.

651
00:37:17,590 --> 00:37:21,094
There was talk that she loved
designer goods and bribes.

652
00:37:21,177 --> 00:37:23,972
How is that related to Baek Yuna's case?

653
00:37:24,055 --> 00:37:25,974
We looked into it.

654
00:37:26,057 --> 00:37:27,267
According to the rumors,

655
00:37:27,350 --> 00:37:30,103
Baek Yuna's mother was the one
who bribed the principal.

656
00:37:30,186 --> 00:37:33,398
Baek Yuna's mother bribed the principal?

657
00:37:33,481 --> 00:37:34,482
Wait,

658
00:37:35,149 --> 00:37:37,986
she became the lead of the festival
after bribing the principal

659
00:37:38,069 --> 00:37:40,572
and had a promising future,
so why did she kill herself?

660
00:37:45,577 --> 00:37:46,578
[♪ music fades]

661
00:37:46,661 --> 00:37:48,496
"I curse you."

662
00:37:48,580 --> 00:37:50,748
I CURSE YOU

663
00:37:50,832 --> 00:37:52,375
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

664
00:37:53,751 --> 00:37:55,169
Was that about Seyeon?

665
00:37:55,253 --> 00:37:57,005
VICTIM, MOON SEYEON, AGE 18

666
00:37:58,882 --> 00:38:00,925
I CURSE YOU, MOON SEYEON
DIE, DIE!

667
00:38:02,927 --> 00:38:03,928
[forensics officer] Detective Joo.

668
00:38:06,890 --> 00:38:08,892
I found something strange.

669
00:38:10,351 --> 00:38:13,062
We're still investigating
the contents that were inside.

670
00:38:17,025 --> 00:38:18,693
I bought it at the Witch's Shop.

671
00:38:18,776 --> 00:38:20,320
It's a trend at school.

672
00:38:20,945 --> 00:38:22,322
We need to meet this witch.

673
00:38:22,405 --> 00:38:23,615
[♪ music fades]

674
00:38:30,872 --> 00:38:33,041
-[toy skeleton chimes]
-Jesus Christ!

675
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,089
What on earth?

676
00:38:40,173 --> 00:38:42,008
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

677
00:38:44,761 --> 00:38:46,179
[owner, in deep voice] Welcome.

678
00:38:46,262 --> 00:38:49,098
OWNER OF THE WITCH'S SHOP
MA HYUNYOUNG

679
00:38:52,185 --> 00:38:53,561
Do you wish to curse someone?

680
00:38:54,479 --> 00:38:56,105
Or know the future?

681
00:38:56,189 --> 00:38:59,275
In this place, you can do it all.

682
00:38:59,359 --> 00:39:01,361
-[clip clicks]
-We're police.

683
00:39:02,654 --> 00:39:05,823
[in normal voice] Gosh,
what brings the police here? [chuckles]

684
00:39:05,907 --> 00:39:09,702
Everything in here might look strange,
but it's just the shop's theme.

685
00:39:10,703 --> 00:39:13,623
They're all just toys. Like this.

686
00:39:13,706 --> 00:39:15,041
[♪ quirky music playing]

687
00:39:15,124 --> 00:39:17,710
A student from
Juyeon Arts High School recently died.

688
00:39:19,253 --> 00:39:21,214
This was among her belongings.

689
00:39:22,882 --> 00:39:24,175
How did she die?

690
00:39:24,258 --> 00:39:26,344
-We're still investigating that.
-[♪ music fades]

691
00:39:26,427 --> 00:39:28,554
-What is this?
-That's...

692
00:39:28,638 --> 00:39:30,515
It's just a way to blow off some steam.

693
00:39:30,598 --> 00:39:31,599
It's really nothing.

694
00:39:34,769 --> 00:39:37,689
Uh, is this a real bone?

695
00:39:37,772 --> 00:39:38,940
[scoffs]

696
00:39:39,023 --> 00:39:42,193
Oh, of course not. It's plastic.
Where would I get real bones?

697
00:39:42,276 --> 00:39:43,653
Yeah, I thought as much.

698
00:39:44,737 --> 00:39:46,572
But do students buy a lot of this stuff?

699
00:39:46,656 --> 00:39:49,075
Business isn't exactly booming,

700
00:39:49,909 --> 00:39:53,079
but a lot of Juyeon Arts students
have been coming since last year.

701
00:39:53,162 --> 00:39:56,124
They buy curse charms
and protective charms.

702
00:39:56,708 --> 00:39:57,709
Mmm.

703
00:39:57,792 --> 00:39:59,085
I'll buy one of these, too.

704
00:39:59,711 --> 00:40:00,712
Sure.

705
00:40:05,383 --> 00:40:06,426
Excuse me.

706
00:40:07,135 --> 00:40:09,637
I need a copy
of your shop's security footage.

707
00:40:10,972 --> 00:40:12,140
[Hyunuong] Sure.

708
00:40:15,935 --> 00:40:17,353
Sorry, but...

709
00:40:18,021 --> 00:40:19,022
this is

710
00:40:19,981 --> 00:40:22,150
my fifth store.

711
00:40:23,776 --> 00:40:26,279
I really can't afford
to go out of business. [chuckles]

712
00:40:26,362 --> 00:40:28,865
You should try changing your theme.

713
00:40:28,948 --> 00:40:32,827
You're too sweet-looking
for a gloomy place like this.

714
00:40:32,910 --> 00:40:34,078
[♪ quirky music playing]

715
00:40:34,162 --> 00:40:35,997
-Should I?
-[Isoo] Yes.

716
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:39,625
This "Good Luck" charm.
I'll buy ten of these.

717
00:40:39,709 --> 00:40:40,793
[gasps]

718
00:40:40,877 --> 00:40:44,047
Gosh, my Flex Cop! [squeals]

719
00:40:44,130 --> 00:40:46,174
-[Isoo] You know me?
-[Hyunuong] Of course I do.

720
00:40:46,257 --> 00:40:48,092
There's no other chaebol this handsome.

721
00:40:48,176 --> 00:40:50,636
Can you sign your autograph here, too?

722
00:40:51,304 --> 00:40:53,473
-On this?
-It's a curse charm. My bad.

723
00:40:53,556 --> 00:40:54,974
[Isoo] Seriously, on a curse charm?

724
00:40:55,058 --> 00:40:56,434
[Hyunuong] I can't let you get cursed.

725
00:40:57,477 --> 00:40:59,771
-I need a pen.
-Right, a pen. [giggles]

726
00:40:59,854 --> 00:41:00,855
[Isoo, softly] Honestly.

727
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:05,359
[♪ music fades]

728
00:41:05,860 --> 00:41:08,404
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL ARTS FESTIVAL D-6

729
00:41:08,488 --> 00:41:12,158
I know you're all having a hard time
after what happened to Seyeon.

730
00:41:13,743 --> 00:41:14,786
However,

731
00:41:15,536 --> 00:41:17,997
the arts festival
must go ahead as planned.

732
00:41:18,706 --> 00:41:20,708
It's also the right thing
to do for Seyeon.

733
00:41:21,375 --> 00:41:24,879
So you must pull yourselves together
and keep practicing.

734
00:41:24,962 --> 00:41:26,130
[all] Yes, ma'am.

735
00:41:26,839 --> 00:41:29,592
You know who's coming
to the festival, don't you?

736
00:41:30,218 --> 00:41:31,844
Deans from arts colleges,

737
00:41:31,928 --> 00:41:34,597
and even the Minister
of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

738
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:36,849
Your futures depend on this.

739
00:41:38,518 --> 00:41:40,061
The lead dancer will be...

740
00:41:40,853 --> 00:41:42,271
[♪ suspenseful piano music playing]

741
00:41:58,621 --> 00:41:59,664
...Song Gaeun.

742
00:42:05,670 --> 00:42:07,213
[♪ music turns ominous]

743
00:42:08,256 --> 00:42:09,715
You can do it, right, Gaeun?

744
00:42:09,799 --> 00:42:11,175
Yes, ma'am.

745
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,806
[♪ music fades]

746
00:42:16,889 --> 00:42:19,267
NATIONAL FORENSIC SERVICE

747
00:42:22,937 --> 00:42:24,147
[exhales sharply]

748
00:42:27,900 --> 00:42:29,527
[muttering]

749
00:42:34,157 --> 00:42:35,491
Jiwon!

750
00:42:36,617 --> 00:42:37,743
What are you doing?

751
00:42:38,703 --> 00:42:39,954
Oh.

752
00:42:40,037 --> 00:42:41,622
Experimenting.

753
00:42:41,706 --> 00:42:42,790
What?

754
00:42:44,625 --> 00:42:45,835
Ah...

755
00:42:46,627 --> 00:42:47,670
Look at this.

756
00:42:47,753 --> 00:42:49,714
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

757
00:42:52,175 --> 00:42:53,718
These wounds

758
00:42:54,302 --> 00:42:56,053
don't look like cuts from a blade.

759
00:42:56,929 --> 00:42:58,764
The skin tore when the blade struck her.

760
00:42:59,932 --> 00:43:03,060
This is the same kind of blade
the victim used.

761
00:43:07,398 --> 00:43:08,399
The edge isn't sharp.

762
00:43:09,734 --> 00:43:10,902
The blade didn't cut her.

763
00:43:10,985 --> 00:43:13,487
It struck her and tore her skin.

764
00:43:14,155 --> 00:43:17,158
But the angle seemed a little odd,

765
00:43:17,241 --> 00:43:18,826
so I was trying it out myself.

766
00:43:19,619 --> 00:43:20,620
See?

767
00:43:22,663 --> 00:43:23,831
It looks the same, right?

768
00:43:28,002 --> 00:43:29,420
Uh...

769
00:43:29,503 --> 00:43:31,297
-Then...
-Yes.

770
00:43:33,799 --> 00:43:35,301
She did this to herself.

771
00:43:36,219 --> 00:43:37,470
Given the angle,

772
00:43:38,596 --> 00:43:39,597
it was self-inflicted.

773
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:41,515
-[blunt thudding]
-[screaming]

774
00:43:45,853 --> 00:43:48,814
Can someone die from wounds like these?

775
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:50,441
No.

776
00:43:51,150 --> 00:43:53,027
The victim had asthma.

777
00:43:53,653 --> 00:43:57,281
An asthma attack narrowed her airways,
which deprived her of oxygen.

778
00:43:57,907 --> 00:43:59,533
That led to cardiac arrest.

779
00:44:01,994 --> 00:44:06,332
Also, we found
an unidentified metabolite in her blood,

780
00:44:06,415 --> 00:44:09,252
but we need to look into that further.

781
00:44:10,169 --> 00:44:11,212
Okay.

782
00:44:11,295 --> 00:44:12,463
[♪ music swells]

783
00:44:15,007 --> 00:44:16,217
[♪ music fades]

784
00:44:18,678 --> 00:44:20,304
PARK JUNYOUNG
INCOMING CALL

785
00:44:23,224 --> 00:44:24,809
[Junyoung, over car audio] Hey, are you
with Detective Joo?

786
00:44:24,892 --> 00:44:26,185
Yes, go ahead.

787
00:44:26,269 --> 00:44:27,937
The autopsy results are out.

788
00:44:28,020 --> 00:44:30,481
She went into cardiac arrest
from an asthma attack.

789
00:44:30,564 --> 00:44:31,857
[Isoo] What?

790
00:44:31,941 --> 00:44:33,484
What about the cuts on her legs?

791
00:44:33,567 --> 00:44:36,529
They seem self-inflicted.

792
00:44:37,321 --> 00:44:39,282
She did that to herself? Why?

793
00:44:39,365 --> 00:44:40,658
[Junyoung] I don't know,

794
00:44:40,741 --> 00:44:44,120
but the angle suggests
she struck herself and the skin tore.

795
00:44:44,704 --> 00:44:48,124
They also found an unusual metabolite.
They'll analyze it and let us know.

796
00:44:48,207 --> 00:44:50,376
Okay, great job.

797
00:44:50,459 --> 00:44:51,502
Okay.

798
00:44:52,128 --> 00:44:53,296
[Hyera] Wait, Detective Park.

799
00:44:54,130 --> 00:44:56,841
Can you check Baek Yuna's case again?

800
00:44:56,924 --> 00:45:00,052
Start with the security guard.
The security cameras keep bothering me.

801
00:45:00,136 --> 00:45:02,138
-[Junyoung] Okay, got it.
-[line disconnects]

802
00:45:02,722 --> 00:45:05,558
Did Baek Yuna really curse Moon Seyeon?

803
00:45:05,641 --> 00:45:07,059
[♪ tense music playing]

804
00:45:09,228 --> 00:45:11,731
Turn the car around.
I need to see the principal.

805
00:45:11,814 --> 00:45:13,607
What am I, your chauffeur?

806
00:45:13,691 --> 00:45:14,900
You can turn around there.

807
00:45:14,984 --> 00:45:18,070
Yes, ma'am, all right.

808
00:45:18,154 --> 00:45:19,405
[engine revs]

809
00:45:19,488 --> 00:45:20,614
[♪ music fades]

810
00:45:20,698 --> 00:45:22,575
JUYEON ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

811
00:45:22,658 --> 00:45:23,701
[Juhee] Yuna...

812
00:45:25,411 --> 00:45:27,038
was such a promising student.

813
00:45:27,830 --> 00:45:31,667
You don't know how heartbroken I was
when she died like that.

814
00:45:31,751 --> 00:45:34,670
Why would she have taken her own life?

815
00:45:35,463 --> 00:45:37,131
I don't know.

816
00:45:38,132 --> 00:45:41,010
She did seem a little depressed
from before the incident,

817
00:45:41,093 --> 00:45:43,888
but no matter how much I asked,
she wouldn't tell me.

818
00:45:45,681 --> 00:45:47,767
We heard there were rumors

819
00:45:48,934 --> 00:45:50,853
that Baek Yuna's mother gave you a bribe.

820
00:45:51,520 --> 00:45:52,563
[sighs wearily]

821
00:45:52,646 --> 00:45:54,774
[inhales] That's a misunderstanding.

822
00:45:54,857 --> 00:45:57,068
It was a donation for the arts festival,

823
00:45:57,151 --> 00:46:00,112
but people who like to gossip
spread those ridiculous rumors.

824
00:46:00,196 --> 00:46:01,405
What about Seyeon?

825
00:46:02,948 --> 00:46:06,327
The students believe
you received a bribe from her.

826
00:46:06,911 --> 00:46:08,412
[sighs softly, inhales]

827
00:46:09,038 --> 00:46:11,415
They're too young to know any better.

828
00:46:12,124 --> 00:46:13,167
You see, Seyeon

829
00:46:13,876 --> 00:46:15,669
came from a low-income family.

830
00:46:15,753 --> 00:46:17,546
She also had asthma,

831
00:46:17,630 --> 00:46:20,299
so she had a hard time
practicing with the other students.

832
00:46:20,883 --> 00:46:22,843
She had a lot of potential,

833
00:46:22,927 --> 00:46:25,137
so I picked her as the lead dancer

834
00:46:25,221 --> 00:46:27,181
and allowed her to practice on her own.

835
00:46:33,062 --> 00:46:35,606
What happened to Seyeon?

836
00:46:35,689 --> 00:46:37,900
It seems she died from an asthma attack.

837
00:46:38,484 --> 00:46:40,027
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

838
00:46:40,111 --> 00:46:42,279
We came to tell you
that this wasn't a murder.

839
00:46:42,863 --> 00:46:44,198
[exhales sharply]

840
00:46:44,281 --> 00:46:47,743
Then what happened to her legs?

841
00:46:47,827 --> 00:46:49,495
[Isoo] Mmm.

842
00:46:49,578 --> 00:46:50,579
That

843
00:46:51,288 --> 00:46:54,125
might be Baek Yuna's curse.

844
00:46:54,792 --> 00:46:57,586
Uh, this is just my unofficial opinion.

845
00:46:57,670 --> 00:46:58,963
What are you talking about?

846
00:46:59,547 --> 00:47:01,882
[inhales sharply] This school

847
00:47:01,966 --> 00:47:04,635
is filled with the energy of a curse.

848
00:47:10,266 --> 00:47:11,308
Uh...

849
00:47:12,059 --> 00:47:13,060
What's this?

850
00:47:14,061 --> 00:47:15,438
Have you never seen it before?

851
00:47:16,272 --> 00:47:17,982
It's a trend among the students.

852
00:47:18,524 --> 00:47:19,859
It's a curse pouch.

853
00:47:19,942 --> 00:47:21,944
The students carry this around?

854
00:47:22,027 --> 00:47:23,487
No.

855
00:47:24,447 --> 00:47:26,449
They secretly slip the curse in.

856
00:47:27,491 --> 00:47:29,827
My gosh, how could they do such a thing?

857
00:47:34,707 --> 00:47:35,708
[exhales softly]

858
00:47:37,293 --> 00:47:38,919
[♪ music increases in tempo]

859
00:47:52,183 --> 00:47:53,767
[♪ music turns ominous]

860
00:47:53,851 --> 00:47:55,603
SONG GAEUN

861
00:48:01,025 --> 00:48:02,401
[intercom chimes]

862
00:48:05,905 --> 00:48:06,906
Oh.

863
00:48:06,989 --> 00:48:09,325
I'm with Gangha Police.
You remember me, right?

864
00:48:10,034 --> 00:48:11,118
Yes.

865
00:48:11,202 --> 00:48:13,370
May I come in for a second?

866
00:48:14,079 --> 00:48:15,080
Sure.

867
00:48:22,338 --> 00:48:24,840
Did I do something wrong?

868
00:48:27,426 --> 00:48:30,679
Uh, a student died
at school last fall, right?

869
00:48:30,763 --> 00:48:32,056
Yes.

870
00:48:32,806 --> 00:48:33,849
Back then,

871
00:48:37,019 --> 00:48:39,271
-why did you do it?
-What?

872
00:48:39,355 --> 00:48:41,190
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

873
00:48:42,900 --> 00:48:44,109
Why did you do it?

874
00:48:53,410 --> 00:48:55,204
Because I was scared.

875
00:48:55,287 --> 00:48:56,705
Of what?

876
00:48:56,789 --> 00:48:59,124
I was the only person at school.

877
00:49:00,125 --> 00:49:02,836
I was worried I'd become a suspect.

878
00:49:02,920 --> 00:49:03,921
It's not too late.

879
00:49:04,004 --> 00:49:05,339
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

880
00:49:05,422 --> 00:49:07,550
Tell me everything

881
00:49:08,300 --> 00:49:09,677
right from the beginning.

882
00:49:13,556 --> 00:49:18,102
At night, the student's mother turned up,
saying her daughter was missing.

883
00:49:18,185 --> 00:49:20,020
SEVEN MONTHS AGO

884
00:49:21,939 --> 00:49:23,232
[exclaims in horror]

885
00:49:24,066 --> 00:49:25,150
[sobbing]

886
00:49:25,693 --> 00:49:27,319
[security guard] But she was dead.

887
00:49:28,445 --> 00:49:31,073
The police came
and asked for the security footage,

888
00:49:31,490 --> 00:49:32,658
but the cameras were off.

889
00:49:33,951 --> 00:49:35,077
So,

890
00:49:36,870 --> 00:49:38,163
I lied

891
00:49:39,248 --> 00:49:41,917
that they'd been down for a few days.

892
00:49:43,669 --> 00:49:45,296
But I thought it was a suicide.

893
00:49:46,171 --> 00:49:47,840
It's hard to say now.

894
00:49:47,923 --> 00:49:51,385
You said the cameras weren't down.
Someone turned them off.

895
00:49:51,468 --> 00:49:52,511
I mean,

896
00:49:53,637 --> 00:49:57,516
I don't know if they were turned off
or if I pressed the wrong button.

897
00:49:57,600 --> 00:50:00,227
I was still new to the job back then.

898
00:50:01,562 --> 00:50:02,771
I swear, no one was there.

899
00:50:02,855 --> 00:50:05,566
When did you realize the cameras were off?

900
00:50:06,900 --> 00:50:10,321
I found out after the police arrived,
so it was near midnight.

901
00:50:10,404 --> 00:50:12,281
When did you last see them on?

902
00:50:12,364 --> 00:50:16,702
I went to do my rounds at 10:00 p.m.,
and they were working fine then.

903
00:50:16,785 --> 00:50:19,204
[♪ music swells, fades]

904
00:50:19,288 --> 00:50:20,456
[sighs softly]

905
00:50:21,248 --> 00:50:23,208
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

906
00:50:32,551 --> 00:50:35,763
If someone turned off
the security cameras...

907
00:50:35,846 --> 00:50:38,307
Was Baek Yuna murdered?

908
00:50:39,308 --> 00:50:41,352
Any luck reaching Baek Yuna's parents?

909
00:50:41,435 --> 00:50:44,521
No. They both moved abroad,
and I can't get a hold of them.

910
00:50:45,314 --> 00:50:46,732
[breathes deeply]

911
00:50:48,651 --> 00:50:50,778
Let's focus on Moon Seyeon's case first.

912
00:50:50,861 --> 00:50:51,862
Okay.

913
00:50:52,863 --> 00:50:56,408
But this seems like an accident,
not a crime.

914
00:50:57,576 --> 00:51:00,079
-We'll have to find out.
-How?

915
00:51:00,746 --> 00:51:02,331
-I know an expert.
-[♪ music fades]

916
00:51:02,414 --> 00:51:04,375
-Kyungjin, let's go.
-Okay.

917
00:51:08,128 --> 00:51:09,254
[door opens]

918
00:51:13,300 --> 00:51:15,052
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

919
00:51:16,428 --> 00:51:18,180
You're asking if this is a real curse?

920
00:51:18,263 --> 00:51:19,640
-Yes.
-Yes.

921
00:51:21,183 --> 00:51:22,601
-[shaman] Mmm.
-[bells jangling]

922
00:51:33,195 --> 00:51:34,446
[♪ music fades]

923
00:51:34,530 --> 00:51:35,531
It's not.

924
00:51:36,281 --> 00:51:38,784
This poor child
is no longer in this world.

925
00:51:39,785 --> 00:51:41,286
She has already left.

926
00:51:41,870 --> 00:51:45,374
Ah. Then what about this student?

927
00:51:50,295 --> 00:51:51,505
Another one died?

928
00:51:52,131 --> 00:51:55,592
Yes, another student died
in the exact same place.

929
00:51:58,429 --> 00:51:59,596
[sighs deeply]

930
00:52:00,055 --> 00:52:01,181
[bells jangling]

931
00:52:02,015 --> 00:52:04,059
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music playing]

932
00:52:13,402 --> 00:52:15,154
[screeching eerily]

933
00:52:17,740 --> 00:52:19,575
[♪ music swells]

934
00:52:19,658 --> 00:52:20,826
[♪ music resumes tempo]

935
00:52:20,909 --> 00:52:22,703
She's still at the school.

936
00:52:22,786 --> 00:52:25,038
A vengeful spirit is there.

937
00:52:28,041 --> 00:52:29,209
[grunts softly]

938
00:52:29,877 --> 00:52:31,336
[♪ percussive folk music playing]

939
00:52:36,925 --> 00:52:37,926
[spectral exhale]

940
00:52:42,306 --> 00:52:43,557
[spectral exhale]

941
00:52:43,640 --> 00:52:45,559
[♪ eerie, suspenseful music continues]

942
00:52:45,642 --> 00:52:46,977
-[shaman] What is that?
-[spectral exhale]

943
00:52:48,729 --> 00:52:50,105
[♪ music turns ominous]

944
00:52:51,231 --> 00:52:52,483
[♪ music swells]

945
00:52:55,027 --> 00:52:56,153
[♪ music fades]

946
00:52:57,821 --> 00:52:58,822
[exhales softly]

947
00:52:58,906 --> 00:53:00,365
What is it?

948
00:53:00,449 --> 00:53:03,243
An item with fur, about this big.

949
00:53:03,327 --> 00:53:04,620
She left it behind.

950
00:53:04,703 --> 00:53:05,746
[whispering] What could it be?

951
00:53:07,790 --> 00:53:09,500
Why is your mind so troubled?

952
00:53:10,250 --> 00:53:11,251
[chuckles]

953
00:53:11,877 --> 00:53:13,128
You got dumped by a girl.

954
00:53:14,379 --> 00:53:15,506
[Kyungjin gasps]

955
00:53:18,050 --> 00:53:19,051
How did you know?

956
00:53:19,676 --> 00:53:21,887
Call her. She's waiting for you.

957
00:53:21,970 --> 00:53:24,097
What? Right now?

958
00:53:24,181 --> 00:53:25,933
Are you going to let
a good woman get away?

959
00:53:26,016 --> 00:53:27,434
No.

960
00:53:30,729 --> 00:53:31,980
[Isoo chuckles]

961
00:53:32,689 --> 00:53:33,732
[shaman] Detective Jin.

962
00:53:34,691 --> 00:53:35,818
Yes?

963
00:53:35,901 --> 00:53:38,403
I have a feeling something bad
is going to happen soon.

964
00:53:40,030 --> 00:53:41,698
-To me?
-Yes.

965
00:53:41,782 --> 00:53:43,033
[♪ melancholy music playing]

966
00:53:43,116 --> 00:53:45,577
Misfortune and trouble
with the law await you.

967
00:53:46,245 --> 00:53:47,663
I see blood.

968
00:53:52,209 --> 00:53:53,210
Be careful.

969
00:53:53,919 --> 00:53:56,129
Someone is after you.

970
00:53:56,213 --> 00:53:58,674
You mustn't open the door.

971
00:54:03,720 --> 00:54:04,847
[♪ music fades]

972
00:54:10,853 --> 00:54:12,938
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

973
00:54:36,295 --> 00:54:37,379
[exhales softly]

974
00:54:38,881 --> 00:54:40,048
[sighs heavily]

975
00:54:45,178 --> 00:54:46,346
[sighs softly]

976
00:54:47,514 --> 00:54:48,682
[grunts]

977
00:54:52,436 --> 00:54:54,396
[♪ pleasant music plays, fades]

978
00:55:00,694 --> 00:55:02,195
[birds chirping]

979
00:55:02,279 --> 00:55:03,405
[sighs softly]

980
00:55:14,708 --> 00:55:16,209
[♪ ominous music playing]

981
00:55:38,023 --> 00:55:39,900
[♪ ticking, ominous music playing]

982
00:55:46,323 --> 00:55:47,866
[♪ music swells]

983
00:55:53,246 --> 00:55:54,247
[♪ music fades]

984
00:55:54,331 --> 00:55:55,666
[cell phone vibrating]

985
00:55:56,249 --> 00:55:57,292
Mmm.

986
00:55:58,335 --> 00:55:59,795
-Hello?
-[Isoo] Doctor.

987
00:56:00,420 --> 00:56:03,215
I just woke up and my house is a wreck.

988
00:56:05,217 --> 00:56:07,427
[sighs] I don't remember anything
about this.

989
00:56:08,637 --> 00:56:11,556
Does the medication I'm on
have any side effects?

990
00:56:11,640 --> 00:56:14,601
[psychiatrist] No, the medication
you're currently taking is very safe.

991
00:56:14,685 --> 00:56:18,146
You might feel a little dizzy,
but there are no serious side effects.

992
00:56:18,230 --> 00:56:21,149
Could a burglar have broken in?

993
00:56:21,233 --> 00:56:23,944
No. No one can get in here.

994
00:56:24,945 --> 00:56:26,196
And nothing's been stolen.

995
00:56:26,905 --> 00:56:29,449
-Would you like to come in to see me?
-Yes, all right.

996
00:56:31,034 --> 00:56:32,077
[line disconnects]

997
00:56:32,160 --> 00:56:33,620
[♪ ominous music playing]

998
00:56:37,833 --> 00:56:39,000
[♪ music fades]

999
00:56:42,421 --> 00:56:43,755
Hey, Detective Joo.

1000
00:56:45,507 --> 00:56:46,508
Have a look at this.

1001
00:56:47,217 --> 00:56:48,844
This red thing here.

1002
00:56:49,428 --> 00:56:50,429
It's a drug.

1003
00:56:50,512 --> 00:56:52,514
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1004
00:56:52,597 --> 00:56:53,807
-A drug?
-Yes.

1005
00:56:53,890 --> 00:56:56,643
I've never seen it before.
Narcotics are looking into it.

1006
00:56:56,727 --> 00:56:58,729
-I'll let you know once I know more.
-Okay.

1007
00:56:59,354 --> 00:57:00,814
-Take care.
-Okay.

1008
00:57:06,278 --> 00:57:08,196
[line connects, ringing]

1009
00:57:08,280 --> 00:57:09,281
[Dr. Yoon] Hello?

1010
00:57:10,031 --> 00:57:12,284
That metabolite found
in Moon Seyeon's blood.

1011
00:57:12,367 --> 00:57:13,577
Ah.

1012
00:57:13,660 --> 00:57:15,120
The lab results came back.

1013
00:57:15,203 --> 00:57:17,539
-It's a drug.
-What kind of drug is it?

1014
00:57:17,622 --> 00:57:20,876
[sighs] I think this is the first time
it's turned up in Korea.

1015
00:57:20,959 --> 00:57:23,879
You know that case overseas
when someone was paralyzed

1016
00:57:23,962 --> 00:57:26,256
-after touching a bill on the ground?
-Yes.

1017
00:57:26,339 --> 00:57:28,008
It's a similar kind of drug.

1018
00:57:28,091 --> 00:57:30,051
It causes hallucinations in most people,

1019
00:57:30,135 --> 00:57:33,597
but the victim had asthma,
so it triggered an attack.

1020
00:57:33,680 --> 00:57:34,848
[♪ music swells]

1021
00:57:37,267 --> 00:57:38,351
[♪ music fades]

1022
00:57:39,394 --> 00:57:40,729
There was a drug?

1023
00:57:41,646 --> 00:57:42,647
[Hyera] Yes.

1024
00:57:44,399 --> 00:57:46,735
Someone slipped this drug
into Seyeon's bag...

1025
00:57:46,818 --> 00:57:48,487
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

1026
00:57:48,570 --> 00:57:50,781
...and it made her hallucinate.

1027
00:57:50,864 --> 00:57:52,949
That triggered an asthma attack
and she died.

1028
00:57:53,033 --> 00:57:56,077
Did someone put this drug in to kill her?

1029
00:57:57,037 --> 00:57:59,331
It might have been
to take the lead role from her.

1030
00:58:00,582 --> 00:58:04,336
They might not have known
it was dangerous for someone with asthma.

1031
00:58:04,419 --> 00:58:07,422
They put a curse pouch in her bag?

1032
00:58:07,506 --> 00:58:09,216
It must've happened at school.

1033
00:58:09,299 --> 00:58:10,300
Yes.

1034
00:58:11,510 --> 00:58:13,470
The culprit would've left a trace.

1035
00:58:13,553 --> 00:58:15,013
-Call in a drug-sniffing dog.
-Got it.

1036
00:58:15,096 --> 00:58:16,097
[♪ music fades]

1037
00:58:30,904 --> 00:58:31,905
[bag unzips]

1038
00:58:34,699 --> 00:58:36,451
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1039
00:59:11,361 --> 00:59:13,154
[breathes heavily]

1040
00:59:15,073 --> 00:59:17,200
-[♪ ominous sting]
-[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

1041
00:59:17,284 --> 00:59:18,451
[exhales shakily]

1042
00:59:18,869 --> 00:59:19,911
[Juhee] Good morning.

1043
00:59:22,163 --> 00:59:23,498
Is everyone here?

1044
00:59:26,710 --> 00:59:28,378
All right, get into formation.

1045
00:59:36,136 --> 00:59:38,013
[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

1046
00:59:41,349 --> 00:59:42,475
[brakes squeal]

1047
00:59:48,565 --> 00:59:49,941
All right.

1048
00:59:50,025 --> 00:59:51,109
Get ready!

1049
00:59:51,192 --> 00:59:52,402
[♪ music fades]

1050
00:59:56,364 --> 00:59:57,616
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

1051
00:59:57,699 --> 00:59:59,117
[blade swooshing]

1052
01:00:10,879 --> 01:00:12,297
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1053
01:00:12,881 --> 01:00:14,132
[barking]

1054
01:00:18,720 --> 01:00:20,263
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1055
01:00:25,685 --> 01:00:28,229
[high-pitched tone droning, fades]

1056
01:00:30,815 --> 01:00:32,233
[blade swooshing]

1057
01:00:50,752 --> 01:00:52,545
[spectral breathing]

1058
01:00:55,173 --> 01:00:56,716
[♪ music swells]

1059
01:01:01,137 --> 01:01:02,597
[Gaeun panting]

1060
01:01:02,681 --> 01:01:03,682
[♪ music fades]

1061
01:01:03,765 --> 01:01:05,767
[panting, breath trembling]

1062
01:01:05,850 --> 01:01:07,560
-[stick taps twice]
-What are you doing?

1063
01:01:07,644 --> 01:01:09,396
[Gaeun, breath trembling]

1064
01:01:10,105 --> 01:01:12,315
Gaeun, what's wrong?

1065
01:01:12,399 --> 01:01:13,525
[breathing frantically]

1066
01:01:13,608 --> 01:01:14,734
[breathing slowing, trembling]

1067
01:01:14,818 --> 01:01:16,361
[♪ ominous music playing]

1068
01:01:17,570 --> 01:01:19,406
[spectral breathing]

1069
01:01:21,449 --> 01:01:22,993
[Seyeon] I'm the lead dancer.

1070
01:01:26,287 --> 01:01:27,998
[slow, heavy, distorted breathing]

1071
01:01:41,094 --> 01:01:43,430
-[Yuna] I'm the lead dancer.
-[Seyeon] I'm the lead dancer.

1072
01:01:43,513 --> 01:01:45,432
-[Yuna] I'm the lead dancer.
-[Seyeon] I'm the lead dancer.

1073
01:01:50,103 --> 01:01:51,980
[spectral murmuring]

1074
01:01:53,356 --> 01:01:55,442
[♪ music swells]

1075
01:01:58,153 --> 01:01:59,571
[distorted screaming]

1076
01:01:59,654 --> 01:02:00,989
[sharp swoosh, slash]

1077
01:02:01,072 --> 01:02:02,198
[♪ music slows]

1078
01:02:03,241 --> 01:02:05,076
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1079
01:02:06,995 --> 01:02:09,330
[Gaeun breathing heavily, distorted]

1080
01:02:16,379 --> 01:02:17,672
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1081
01:02:19,924 --> 01:02:21,551
[♪ music swells]

1082
01:02:24,345 --> 01:02:25,388
[♪ music fades]

1083
01:02:25,472 --> 01:02:26,473
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 9

1084
01:02:26,556 --> 01:02:28,058
WHAT'S THE TRUTH BEHIND THE CURSE?

1085
01:02:28,141 --> 01:02:30,143
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

1086
01:02:45,658 --> 01:02:49,079
Special Cast. Joo Hyunyoung

1087
01:02:49,162 --> 01:02:52,582
Special Cast. Jeon Hyebin

1088
01:03:04,302 --> 01:03:05,720
A curse pouch had drugs inside.

1089
01:03:05,804 --> 01:03:08,264
[Juhee] Are you saying one of my students
did something like that?

1090
01:03:08,348 --> 01:03:09,516
Can we talk for a moment?

1091
01:03:09,599 --> 01:03:10,642
Where would I get drugs?

1092
01:03:10,725 --> 01:03:12,227
[Hyera] Did you find anything
on Seyeon's phone?

1093
01:03:12,310 --> 01:03:14,229
[shaman] An item with fur, about this big.

1094
01:03:14,312 --> 01:03:15,939
The shaman said she saw this.

1095
01:03:16,022 --> 01:03:17,857
This is a video app.

1096
01:03:17,941 --> 01:03:19,442
You can't do this.

1097
01:03:19,526 --> 01:03:21,820
-[students gasp]
-[Hayun] I was only messing around.

1098
01:03:21,903 --> 01:03:23,404
But how did you know?

1099
01:03:23,488 --> 01:03:24,572
Let's do this!

1100
01:03:24,656 --> 01:03:26,616
Did Isoo side with Joo Hyera?

1101
01:03:26,699 --> 01:03:28,243
[Minjae] Yu Seongwon brought a woman over.

1102
01:03:28,326 --> 01:03:30,745
-[Hyera] We have no way of watching him.
-[car horn honking]

1103
01:03:30,829 --> 01:03:32,664
What was the worst thing you've ever done?

1104
01:03:32,747 --> 01:03:33,748
What about you?

1105
01:03:33,832 --> 01:03:36,376
The worst thing I've done?

1106
01:03:36,459 --> 01:03:37,627
You'd be shocked if you knew.

1107
01:03:37,710 --> 01:03:39,212
How do you want to die?

1108
01:03:39,295 --> 01:03:40,630
[♪ music fades]

1109
01:03:44,259 --> 01:03:45,677
Why do you take photographs?

1110
01:03:46,761 --> 01:03:48,638
To feel you while I work.

1111
01:03:48,721 --> 01:03:49,931
[♪ foreboding music playing]

1112
01:03:50,014 --> 01:03:51,850
Can I get a copy if they come out well?

1113
01:03:53,184 --> 01:03:54,352
[chuckles softly]

1114
01:03:54,435 --> 01:03:55,436
No.

1115
01:03:58,439 --> 01:04:00,775
What kind of artwork
are you going to make me into?

1116
01:04:00,859 --> 01:04:02,861
I'm not sure. [sighs softly]

1117
01:04:02,944 --> 01:04:04,612
I can't say I know you yet.

1118
01:04:04,696 --> 01:04:06,030
What do you like most?

1119
01:04:06,114 --> 01:04:08,491
I like painting the most.

1120
01:04:09,993 --> 01:04:11,661
I wish I could

1121
01:04:12,453 --> 01:04:15,081
spend just one month painting,
without worrying about money.

1122
01:04:16,082 --> 01:04:17,167
[scoffs]

1123
01:04:18,168 --> 01:04:19,377
That's no fun.

1124
01:04:19,961 --> 01:04:21,504
What's no fun?

1125
01:04:28,178 --> 01:04:29,387
[exhales softly]

1126
01:04:30,972 --> 01:04:32,182
Want a glass of champagne?

1127
01:04:32,891 --> 01:04:34,893
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
